 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Simultaneous actions",
     "texto": [
      "**V-(으)며** can indicate that two actions happen at the same time: 웃다 → **웃으며** (while smiling), 먹다 → **먹으며** (while eating). **-며** is added after a vowel and **-으며** after a consonant; with irregular ㄷ, ㄷ changes to ㄹ: 걷다 → **걸으며**. It is used mostly in a careful or written register.",
      "학생들이 웃으며 이야기해요 = the students talk while smiling."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Listing features",
     "texto": [
      "It also links parallel features or facts, like «and also»: 이 지역은 교통이 편리하며 관광지도 많아요 = this area has convenient transport and many tourist spots too. The context determines whether simultaneity or enumeration predominates.",
      "It is not usually the most natural option for every «and» in informal conversation."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
